+**IDEAL-W⁺ narrowing note (2026-11-16; HQ D78 correctness event; outside every registered statement span).** The conclusions at `:27-33` now state delivery in two clauses, in the form of W2-UNI's Proposition F-UNI v2 (`Theory_work/Wave2/W2-UNI/lemmas/L5_delivery.md`): (a) under IDEAL-W, P(no output) = 0 only on the bounded domain 𝔇; (b) for every admissible n, and every asymptotic delivery conclusion, under A:IDEAL-W⁺. Reason (Sol review TR1, `Theory_work/Dept/research/FUNI_transfer/TR1_sol.md` §1–§2): two shipped LS0 cap validators lie outside Theorem D's exit walk and can end an SMC-branch fit without output, independently of resources: `le > 1e6` (`Scripts/SMC_BVS/core/v3_run.R:96-97`; le = ℓ_n in the stated configuration) and `cap_ll > numeric_limits<int>::max()` with cap_ll = ℓ_n + |S̃₀| (`Scripts/SMC_BVS/core/cpp/v3_core.cpp:474`). IDEAL-W (C-DLV `STATEMENT.md:24-25`, unchanged) excludes overflow, not these application-level rejection predicates. On 𝔇 neither predicate fires: ℓ_n ≤ ℓ_raw ≤ 10⁶ (p ≤ p_raw) and ℓ_n + |S̃₀| ≤ ℓ_raw + K_n ≤ ℓ_raw + ⌊n/2⌋ ≤ 2³¹ − 1; the exact-enumeration branch reaches neither check. 𝔇 is sufficient, not necessary, and bounded, so clause (a) carries no asymptotic conclusion. Under A:IDEAL-W⁺ both predicates are false. In both clauses the no-output step of the proof (Theorem D's exit walk with the total tier-1 fallback and the stated allocation) is otherwise unchanged (TR1 §1 table). A2 concerns the method as specified at A1 (A2 `:5`, `:9`; LS0 was not then shipped, A3 finding 4); its allocation contains Corollary R's preflight bounds but not A4's LS0 preflight terms P_e + A and P̄_LS0, which the shipped preflight additionally charges (FIN `s6_delivery.tex:37-44`); this note does not add them (open item for HQ). Definition (verbatim; registered assumption A:IDEAL-W⁺):
+
+**A:IDEAL-W⁺ (IDEAL-W with the two LS0 cap ceilings lifted).** IDEAL-W, exactly as defined in C-DLV `STATEMENT.md:24-25`, and the two shipped rejection predicates `le > 10⁶` (`Scripts/SMC_BVS/core/v3_run.R:96`, the LS0 base-cap validator; le = ℓ_n = ⌈log₂(n + p + 1)⌉ in the shipped configuration) and `ℓ + |S̃₀| > INT_MAX` (`Scripts/SMC_BVS/core/cpp/v3_core.cpp:474`, the disjunct `cap_ll > numeric_limits<int>::max()` of the LS0 cap-range guard, `int` read as unbounded) are false. Nothing else is lifted: the other conditions of those two validators (numeric type, length, finiteness, integrality, `le < 0`, `o.ls0_ell < 0`), every other validator, the 10⁶-maximiser start-mode enumeration cap with its tie-aware DP fallback, and every fallback and method cap are kept as coded. Like IDEAL-W and EX-A, A:IDEAL-W⁺ is an idealisation of the machine and code; a larger allocation does not imply it.
